    {
      "calls": [
        {
          "ID": "toolu_01YWoVCHKkBKgbb3XQweqXhQ",
          "Name": "submit_read",
          "Input": {
            "assessments": [
              {
                "facts": [
                  "F79",
                  "F80",
                  "F81",
                  "F89",
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S16:F93",
                  "S10:F50",
                  "S14:F56",
                  "S12:F52"
                ],
                "ref": "N1",
                "statement": "The new Prime Minister's domestic agenda in Scotland and on the railways reapplies, at national scale, the Greater Manchester approach he took as Mayor: localised employment support, delivery run from outside London, and public control of transport.",
                "supersedes": ""
              },
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S17:F82",
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S16:F73",
                  "S16:F83"
                ],
                "ref": "N2",
                "statement": "So far the UK–Scottish Government partnership has produced only a small matched-funding project; the larger devolution offers stay untested until the Scottish Government replies, and the National Economic Council meeting with the First Ministers is the first test.",
                "supersedes": ""
              },
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S1:F12",
                  "S1:F13",
                  "S3:F16",
                  "S3:F38",
                  "S2:F33",
                  "S2:F34",
                  "S2:F40"
                ],
                "ref": "N3",
                "statement": "The UK is increasing military and economic pressure on Russia alongside the US-announced energy ceasefire, not making it depend on that ceasefire, which has no confirmed start date.",
                "supersedes": ""
              }
            ],
            "statements": [
              {
                "cites": [
                  "F80",
                  "F79",
                  "F89",
                  "F59"
                ],
                "text": "Read together, this week's domestic Stories are about the man running the country. Andy Burnham entered Downing Street in July. He had left Westminster in 2017 to become the first Mayor of Greater Manchester, and as Mayor he put the buses back under public control."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S16:F93",
                  "F81"
                ],
                "text": "In Scotland he offered DWP devolution, which he described as a model of localised employment support, and pointed to the Number 10 North office he has created. He says the Live Well model he pioneered in Greater Manchester drew on what he learned in Easterhouse."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S10:F50",
                  "S10:F55",
                  "S14:F56",
                  "S12:F52"
                ],
                "text": "On the railways, the headquarters of Great British Railways was unveiled in Derby, with room for up to 450 staff. A £1 billion fleet of trains for the north is to be built at Alstom's Derby site, and fares have been frozen for the first time in 30 years."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "N1"
                ],
                "text": "My judgement is that this is the Manchester approach applied to the whole country: delivery run from outside London and public control of transport, rather than new programmes run from Whitehall. His record should be judged by whether partners take these offers up."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S17:F82",
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S16:F73"
                ],
                "text": "In Scotland, only one offer has been taken up so far: Holyrood will match the UK's £10 million for two defence technical excellence colleges. The Record holds no reply yet to the bigger offers, DWP devolution and joint work through No10 North and the Scotland Office."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S16:F83",
                  "N2"
                ],
                "text": "The first test is the National Economic Council's meeting with the First Ministers of Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland, which was due about two weeks after 16 October."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S8:F85",
                  "S8:F27"
                ],
                "text": "The Scottish pitch also looked ahead to Brussels. In the same speech the Prime Minister said he would seek a new food and farming deal at the UK–EU summit on 20 November."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S1:F12",
                  "S1:F13"
                ],
                "text": "Abroad, President Trump announced a reciprocal energy ceasefire between Russia and Ukraine. Ukraine said it would put it into effect as soon as a start date was confirmed, and the Record still holds no start date."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S3:F16",
                  "S3:F38",
                  "S2:F34",
                  "S2:F40",
                  "S2:F33"
                ],
                "text": "Meanwhile London has tightened the pressure on Russia rather than easing it. New sanctions cover over 90% of Russia's oil-producing capacity, and a full ban on maritime services for Russian LNG exports is planned. The UK is delivering £45 million of surface-to-air missiles, £10 million of them faster, and ministers have been told to draw up further packages."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "N3"
                ],
                "text": "In short, Britain is not waiting on a truce that has no start date; it is building pressure alongside it."
              }
            ],
            "stories": [
              {
                "developments": [
                  "S16:F93",
                  "S16:F73",
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S17:F82",
                  "S10:F50",
                  "S14:F56",
                  "S11:F51"
                ],
                "title": "Burnham government's agenda for devolving power and delivery to the nations and regions"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
